ent": "Exchange information about logic, its principles, and methods in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.  Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Demonstrative Pronouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a <strong>demonstrative pronoun</strong> to point out something specific in a context. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <strong>demonstrative pronouns</strong> can also indicate an object in space or time, and they can be singular or plural.   </br></br>  When an object is near the speaker, we can use <span class=\"strong\">\u201cthis\u201d</span> as a singular noun and <span class=\"strong\">\u201cthese\u201d</span> for plural nouns.   </br></br>  Example.  </br> <li>    <i> I want <strong>this</strong> t-shirt.</i>   </br></br>  <li>   <i> I love <strong>these</strong> gloves in my hands. </i>  </br></br>When there is a distance between the speaker and the object, we can use <span class=\"strong\">\u201cthat\u201d</span> for a singular noun or <span class=\"strong\">\u201cthose\u201d</span> for plural nouns.   </br></br>  Example:   </br></br> <li> <i> I like to buy <strong>that</strong> computer over there! </i> </br></br>  <li>   <i> She needs to buy <strong>those</strong> books about programming.  </i>  </br></br></span>  There are simple rules to use demonstratives correctly:   </br></br>  1. They always identify situations or nouns.   </br></br>  Example:   </br></br> <li> <i>I can't believe <strong>this!</strong> I have a new computer! </i>  </br></br> 2. We use the demonstratives to describe animals, places or things.   </br></br>  Example:   </br></br> <li> <i><strong>These</strong> computers are very old! We need to change them. </i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "That is why the teacher also mentions the artificial intelligence and deduction systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Thank you, that's so nice of you.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Components of Computational Logic", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>Computational logic</strong> refers to the interdisciplinary practice that constructs the fundamentals on computer science. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Computational logic</strong> is very wide. As most of the sciences, it has theoretical and practical elements that are based on mathematics, artificial intelligence, logic and certainly a computational science. </br></br>  Some of the areas that are included in <strong>computational logic</strong> are: </br></br>  <li>Programming Logic</br> <li>Deduction systems</br> <li>Knowledge representation</br> <li>Inference techniques</br> <li>Mathematical logic</br></br>  <strong>Computational logic</strong> is actually the logic of the object that is common in all areas involved. There is a use of logic in all areas that have an application on <strong>computational logic</strong>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Programming logic is the base of programming itself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Computational logic can be confusing because it involves many disciplines.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "programming logic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way all human logic knowledge can be applied to computer programming", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Programming logic is the base of programming itself. It is a group of coherent ideas and reasons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coherent ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is logical and constant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Programming logic is the base of programming itself. It is a group of coherent ideas and reasons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "structure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a system composed of parts that are put together for a purpose ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This science studies the structure, the fundamentals, and use of the human knowledge  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "quantifiable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that can be measured exactly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Logical operations work according to logical principles and quantifiable results.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hard data ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Information that can be demonstrated, it can be numbers or facts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She also says that hard data or concrete evidence construct all.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Artificial Intelligence (AI)", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the capacity of a computer to make decisions and learn similar to humans", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That is why the teacher also mentions the artificial intelligence and deduction systems.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "take